 "answer": "On Windows, Ollama writes its server logs to:\n\n**Folder:** `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Ollama`, which is usually `C:\\Users\\<your-username>\\AppData\\Local\\Ollama`\n\n**File:** `server.log`, which holds the most recent server output. The same folder also contains `app.log` for the tray application.\n\nTo open it in PowerShell:\n\n```powershell\nGet-Content \"$env:LOCALAPPDATA\\Ollama\\server.log\" -Tail 100\n```\n\nI'm not certain how older logs are named after rotation. I believe they are kept with numbered suffixes such as `server-1.log`, but check the folder to confirm.",
